<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.568 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.568 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE AUG 31, 2001</p>
<p>			     $12.502 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.568    Awarded At	99.715	6.500</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.535    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 5.530    86 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.13 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Aug.01</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 03.Sep.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 28.Aug.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  12.502 BLN USD		 CUSIP    912827Z39</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   26.681			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   534.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.500</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  950.00 MLN		     PRICE	 99.715</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    5.530-6.568 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.568</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD DOWN FROM 6.625 PCT AT AUCTION ON 24.JUL.96</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD LOWEST SINCE 6.565 PCT AT AUCTION 30.MAY.96</p>
